 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "InfiniteQueue() starts empty and has no capacity limit. add(value) appends value at the back. poll() removes and returns the front value, or -1 when the queue is empty. getRandom(r) returns, without removing it, the value at position (r mod size) counted from the front (position 0), or -1 when the queue is empty. Randomness is injected: r is a caller-supplied non-negative integer, so a uniform r gives a uniform element. Every method call is answered in call order on one instance; void methods return nothing.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
